          "property_id": "PROP-W5B6-60",
          "title": "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity for tb-022: Can an attacker forge a transaction signature that recovers to a different sender address?",
          "severity": "Critical",
          "mindset": "Boundary Guard",
          "is_boundary_check": true,
          "reachability": {
            "classification": "external-reachable",
            "entry_points": [
              "P2P",
              "Transaction"
            ],
            "attacker_controlled": true,
            "validation_layers": [
              "ECDSA signature recovery",
              "SECP256K1 curve operations"
            ],
            "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
            "notes": "Transaction sender authentication is fundamental to Ethereum security."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Locate the recover_sender function and all code paths that invoke it for transaction validation.\n2. Verify that SECP256K1 signature recovery is used correctly with proper curve parameters.\n3. Test with malformed signature components (r, s, v values outside valid ranges) and verify rejection.\n4. Attempt signature malleability attacks by flipping s-value and verify the same sender is recovered or rejected.\n5. Test with edge cases: zero r or s, r or s equal to curve order n, and invalid recovery id v.\n6. Verify that signature validation occurs before any state-changing operations.\n7. Check for proper handling of EIP-155 chain ID to prevent cross-chain replay attacks.",
          "bug_class": "Authentication Bypass",
          "risk_category": "Spoofing",
          "notes": "Source: PROP-W5B6-60, Trust Boundary: tb-022, Threat: stride-spoofing-tb-022"
        },
        "code_scope": {
